_line_start":489},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Benefit rates","tree_line_end":496,"tree_line_start":493},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \n \nNew rates of UC will apply from the first day of the first assessment period which commences on or \nafter 06.04.26. DMs can find the new rates in the \nbenefit uprating schedule\n and benefit desk aids and \nshould bear them in mind when reading examples in the ADM that contain benefit rates.","tree_line_end":509,"tree_line_start":497},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Housing costs non-dependant contribution","tree_line_end":513,"tree_line_start":510},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3. \n \nWhere a non-dependant lives with the claimant, a contribution may be appropriate. The contribution is \nmade in the form of a deduction from the allowable housing costs\n1\n. Where applicable \n(\nsee ADM F3140\n)\n \nthe rate of deduction is £96.55","tree_line_end":532,"tree_line_start":514},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nUC Regs, Sch 4, para 14(1)","tree_line_end":543,"tree_line_start":533},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Earned income – work allowance","tree_line_end":547,"tree_line_start":544},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4. \n \nThe appropriate work allowance is\n1","tree_line_end":556,"tree_line_start":548},{"depth":2,"role":"Table","text":"1.\n \n Higher work allowance\nAmount\nSingle claimant - \n \nresponsible for a child or qualifying young person and/or \nhas limited capability for work\n£710\nJoint claimants - \n \nresponsible for one or more children or qualifying young \npersons and/or where one or both have limited capability \nfor work\n£710\n2.\n \n Lower work allowance\n \nSingle claimant - \n \nresponsible for one or more children or qualifying young \npersons and/or has limited capability for work\n£427\nJoint claimants - \n \nresponsible for one or more children or qualifying young \npersons and/or where one or both have limited capability \nfor work\n£427","tree_line_end":786,"tree_line_start":557},{"depth":3,"role":"T